<section class="shell band">
  <h2>Four methods, interlocking</h2>
  <p class="intro-wide">Not four alternatives to choose between. They run together, and which
  one leads on a given day is a clinical decision rather than something you pick in advance.</p>
  <div class="pathways">
    <a href="/approach/narm/">
      <h3>NARM</h3>
      <p>Asks what pattern is running, where it was learned, and what choice you have once you
      can see it happening rather than only feel it.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/approach/somatic-experiencing/">
      <h3>Somatic Experiencing</h3>
      <p>Sets the pace your nervous system can hold: shock trauma met a little at a time,
      building your window of tolerance rather than testing it.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/approach/emdr/">
      <h3>EMDR</h3>
      <p>Finishes processing what got stored raw, with stabilization first. What it involves,
      who it suits, and what is usually behind it when it has stalled before.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/approach/ifs-informed-emdr/">
      <h3>IFS-informed EMDR</h3>
      <p>Where most of the work here happens. The protective parts of you are consulted before
      anything is processed, and most of the emphasis sits in that preparation.</p>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--sand">
  <div class="shell">
  <h2>Who this is for</h2>
  <p class="intro-wide">Adults and young adults, including college-age clients; the practice
  does not work with young children. Reem Glasco, LPC-S, sees a small number of them for
  developmental trauma, C-PTSD, anxiety, panic attacks, depression and procrastination.
  {% include "partials/text/session-terms.njk" %}
  Because her caseload is limited by her supervision and consultation work, most new clients
  are seen by the practice's <strong>LPC Associates</strong>, who have openings including at
  sliding-scale fees.</p>
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <p>Alongside the paths above, people come here for life transitions, graduating, leaving,
      arriving, becoming a parent, losing someone, and for self care for mothers, which usually
      starts with permission.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Trail walk, movement and equine sessions are for adults only, in person in central
      Texas, and need a consult plus one to three online sessions first, so we know each other
      before we are outside.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="intro-wide">The paths overlap a great deal, and the consult is where the starting
  point gets chosen.</p>

  </div>
</section>



